  "model": "MODEL-BASED (case-control cohort; no absolute risk is estimated directly): annual progression incidence lambda among NDBE patients; the rule's patient-level sensitivity (progressors caught at >= 1 pre-event endoscopy) and specificity (non-progressors never flagged) are assumed to transport. Progressions per 1,000 patient-years in the de-escalated group = 1000 x lambda (1 - sens) / (lambda (1 - sens) + (1 - lambda) spec). CIs: patient bootstrap (2,000 draws, RandomState(0)) of sens and spec; the bootstrap cannot exceed the cohort's observed misses, so the exact Clopper-Pearson upper limit on the majority-vote miss count is given alongside. Guideline bar (gastro review): <= 2 per 1,000 patient-years (short-segment NDBE, about 0.2%/yr)."
